No generator script found for `docs/agents/generated/pr_review.md`; there's a coverage test that checks generated docs are complete. The hand-sync of both doc files is the existing convention then. Fine — no finding there.

Now let me look at the action()-level filter test (verdict recomputation) to confirm coverage of the ordering, and then quickly verify the demote-file-stamp test. Then I'll compose findings.

Actually, let me also spot-check one more subtle thing in `stampDemotionNotesOnFiles`:

```js
function stampDemotionNotesOnFiles(reviewData, applied, ctx) {
   var inline = filterInlineOf(reviewData);
   var stamps = demoteStampsOf(aplied);
   for each stamp: matchingStampTarget(inline, stamp) → stampOneDemotion(entry, stamp, ctx)
   cleanup __filterNoted
}
``

`isStampTarget(entry, stamp)`: `entry.path !== stamp.path || entry.line !== stamp.line` — stamp.path/line come from the CANDIDATE (`candidate.path` = `c.path || c.file`, `candidate.line`). entry.path is the entry's path. Consistent for path+line matching. Two entries with same path+line: consume-once via `__filterNoted`. If two DIFFERENT entries share path+line and only one was demoted — first match wins, may stamp the wrong one of the two (both same path+line, severity match). Cosmetic ambiguity; same path+line duplicates are degenerate anyway. Skip.

One REAL subtle thing: `demoteOutcomeOf` stamps `entry.severity = v.tier` — so ALL entries demoted in this round have severity == stamp.to. If TWO entries (both same path+line) were demoted to the same tier, only ONE gets the file note (consume-once by design to avoid double-append; but if they reference DIFFERENT comment files, the second file never gets its note!). Wait: matchingStampTarget finds the FIRST unstamped entry matching path+line+severity → stamps its file. Second demote with same path+line but different comment file → matchingStampTarget skips the first (now `__filterNoted`) → finds second → stamps ITS file. OK good — consume-once per ENTRY, not per file. Correct.

But if two demoted entries share the same path+line AND the same comment file (possible? two threads on the same line referencing the same file — unusual) → second entry would ALSO append to the same file → double-append. But consume-once prevents? No — consume-once marks the ENTRY; second entry is a different entry → gets stamped → same file appended twice. Edge of an edge. Skip.

Now — one more important check. **`applyReviewFilter` is called with `ctx` — `ctx.reviewPolicy`.** Where does ctx.reviewPolicy get set? Let me verify it's the RESOLVED policy (validateReviewPolicy output with .verification). grep "ctx.reviewPolicy =".

